WEBVTT

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.080
My, my.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.340
Masaru never gets up before the afternoon on a Sunday.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.900
This must be all thanks to Agu-chan!

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.860
More!

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:20.800
All right.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.230
Just a minute.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.200
Here you are, Agu-chan.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.620
What the hell, Mom?

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:26.770
Serve me before Agumon!

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.000
I never said I wouldn't let you have your share. Just wait for a bit.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.850
After all, Agu-chan's still a child.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.160
What kind of child is this big?

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.370
Gimme that!

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:44.260
I won't hand over the last of Sayuri's fried eggs, not even to you!

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.280
Spit that out!

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.060
Give it back!

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:51.040
No way!

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.300
Stop calling my mom by her first name, too!

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.880
What children.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:06.990
Tohma-sama.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.400
The temperature today is 17 degrees.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.740
It is somewhat warmer than Austria, is it not?

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:25.620
What are you doing, Agu-chan?

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:27.360
Chika!

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.500
Help me get into this basket!

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.090
Okay, but... why?

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:35.300
I don't wanna keep running after Aniki all the time!

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:40.760
What a child...

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:42.450
Damn it...

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:45.960
Have a safe trip!

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.240
C'mon, Aniki!

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.010
You can do it, Aniki!

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:55.710
Why the hell do I have to give you a piggyback ride?

00:01:55.710 --> 00:02:00.680
You're the one who told me, "You're a stuffed toy, so don't move!"

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.850
If you insist...

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:10.220
Uh... what do I press again?

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.820
This? No...

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.040
Reporting from HQ.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.700
We have a Digimon signal.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.860
Where?!

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.280
Area C-7. Can you get there directly?

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.660
Yeah! Leave it to us!

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:22.510
To us!

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.830
So boring...

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.360
Nothing's going on at all...

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.400
Nothing at all!

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:32.460
Yeah...

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.560
Hey, what's wrong with your voice?

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.680
Huh?

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.050
What are you talking about?

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:47.640
What's that?

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:48.750
Found it!

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:50.210
Let's fight!

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.110
Fight...

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:57.670
Aniki!

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:58.800
I'll go!

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.260
Baby Flame!

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.930
My attack didn't do anything!

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:10.710
Aniki, gimme that crackling, exploding thing!

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.090
The Digisoul, right?

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.130
Hang on!

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.410
What's up with this guy?

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.010
He's too light, so my punches can't connect!

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.600
You're not solid enough, damn it!

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.160
If I could just hit you once, I can get Agumon to evolve!

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:41.380
Aniki can't get his Digisoul!

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:47.770
After him, Agumon!

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.010
Okay, Aniki!

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.530
What was that?

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.000
A fire monster and... a lizard?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.520
They're called Digimon.

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.910
You don't need to remember that, though.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.790
Memory erasure completed.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.230
Pursuit route secured.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.260
Let's go, Gaomon.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.820
Yes, Master.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.570
The Genius Who Returned Home, Tohma!

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:23.570
Crush Meramon

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.000
The Genius Who Returned Home, Tohma!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.280
Crush Meramon!

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:25.570
Damn it...

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.030
That thing pissed me off...

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:34.320
Well, I didn't think it would go easily for you from the start...

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.040
That's correct.

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.710
The Digimon is secured.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.880
Wh-Who're you?

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.720
Tohma-sama!

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:49.830
When did you get back?

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.640
This is such a surprise!

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:53.960
I'm so happy!

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:53.960
So am I!

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.470
Who are you?

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:04.590
He just ignored me! What a jerk!

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.580
You bastard!

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.070
You took away my prey!

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:16.520
What, gonna fight?

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:23.880
Captain Satsuma.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:26.860
Tohma H. Norstein.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:30.380
As of today, I'll be taking up my position here in DATS's Japanese subdivision.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:33.610
Good to have you here.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:37.310
I've looked through the written reports...

00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:41.270
and it seems rather peculiar that there are a large number of Digimon detected in this country lately.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.970
His stern-looking profile is so wonderful!

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:44.480
It really is!

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.150
Is the frequency not as high in EU?

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.730
No.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:53.530
It must be because it has a larger area.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:56.120
Hm?

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:00.020
Oh, let me introduce you. This is...

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.500
Hey!

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.100
I don't care if you're called Tohma or Tonma...

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.100
NOTE: <i>Tonma</i> (トンマ) means someone who is an idiot.

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.490
But around here, <i>I'm</i>  your senpai!

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:09.490
NOTE: <i>Senpai</i> (先輩) means a senior member within the same group.

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:15.630
I've only been here for three days, but make sure to call me "Daimon-san" or "Daimon-senpai!"

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.710
Already blazing down the warpath?

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:22.310
Tohma is actually <i>your</i>  senpai, Masaru.

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:29.020
Tohma was a part of the Japanese subdivision until six months ago.

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:32.740
He assisted us in keeping Digimon under control and developing the transportation equipment.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:38.320
When EU's headquarters strongly requested his assistance, he went abroad temporarily.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:41.200
B-But no matter how you look at him, he's the same age as I am...

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:45.990
But Tohma-sama is a genius who graduated at Stockholm University's Institute of Science at age 13!

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.650
And at the top of his class!

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.920
A genius?!

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:54.750
What's more, the Norstein are one of the most prominent noble families in Austria.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.790
He's a prince, so to speak!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.680
A prince...?

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:02.730
As for Tohma's partner, Gaomon...

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:06.730
his battle ability is unsurpassed among the Digimon in DATS.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:09.190
They are truly the strongest pair of partners.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.650
Un...surpass...?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.860
Be sure to get along with each other, as you are colleagues.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:18.920
I think it will be futile to do so, Captain Satsuma.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:23.270
There is not a chance that this person could benefit DATS.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.370
What d'you mean?!

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:32.410
People like him should be dismissed at once.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.880
Say that to my face!

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:37.670
Look into a person's eyes when you're talking!

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:39.290
Very well, then.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:42.270
You and your partner are not suited for DATS.

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:43.850
Tohma!

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:44.570
You...!

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:45.770
Get him, Aniki!

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.740
Really, now.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:54.510
You want to face me with that level of power?

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:56.060
How incredibly pathetic.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.480
What do you mean, "that level?"

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:01.400
How strong does that make you, then?!

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.000
Do I have to answer that?

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.450
Yeah!

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.230
Go on, show me!

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:09.920
Let's see the truth behind all that bragging!

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:18.190
Hey! Put on your headgear!

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:18.930
I don't need it!

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.460
Besides, he's not wearing any!

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:26.100
This is the worst...

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.850
Go ahead, do what you want.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:29.240
You got it.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.770
Take him down, Aniki!

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:40.030
You put all of your faith in power, without using any strategy or tactics.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:41.070
Shut up!

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.150
Why did you join DATS?

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.050
Huh?!

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:48.060
It was so I could win, obviously!

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:49.930
Against who?

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.210
Against strong guys!

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.490
What a boring story.

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.300
DATS has an important mission.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:04.220
Every member has an obligation and responsibility to carry that out.

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.400
Shut up!

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.230
Stop acting all elite!

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:11.990
He's beyond help.

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:18.260
Aniki!

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.150
1!

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.440
2!

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:22.720
3!

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:23.940
4!

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:25.190
5!

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:26.350
6!

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.500
7!

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:28.620
8!

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.860
9!

00:10:29.860 --> 00:10:30.990
10!

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:32.290
Tohma wins!

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:41.200
Rude and vulgar people aren't needed in DATS.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.110
Just like I thought...

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.930
Aniki...

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:44.890
Wait right there...

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:50.350
You really are... spouting a lot...

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:52.520
The match is over.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:54.590
Match?

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.800
What we're having is a serious fight!

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.650
It's not a game!

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:02.530
Tohma-sama!

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:10.870
A fight doesn't end until one side admits defeat!

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:24.170
Damn it...

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:25.590
That bastard...

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.800
You should be happy it was a draw!

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:32.520
Tohma's beaten Olympic champions in the past.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:37.030
Well, I've taken out the leader of the third Minato high school!

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:41.400
Really, the only things worthy of a gold medal around here are your pride and your competitive attitude.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.480
Good grief.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.060
Captain!

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:59.050
There's a Digimon signal found in Area D-82 of the harbor district!

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:01.580
Beginning Digimon analysis!

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.190
Transferring to the monitor!

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.930
That's... PetitMeramon!

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.090
The Digimon signal is multiplying! And continuing to increase!

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:18.450
Their numbers... 36, 48, 62!

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:19.400
Almost 100!

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:26.780
If even a small flame from PetitMeramon's body remains, it has the ability to develop and multiply in a short time.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:30.030
It should have been prevented from doing so earlier...

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.300
This is my fault...

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:41.620
It seems you know what caused this.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:47.180
But to think that it could multiply this much within only a few hours...

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:50.380
Allow me to handle this!

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:51.780
Please leave it to us.

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:54.310
It's up to you, Tohma, Gaomon.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.100
Wait!

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:58.060
Those fireballs are ours to beat!

00:12:58.430 --> 00:12:59.310
They're ours!

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:04.240
Are you 100% sure you can secure those Digimon?

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.310
Damn right!

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.520
We'll pull it off somehow using our spirits!

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.160
I will handle it.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:17.170
You think you can do it?! Against that many?

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:19.130
Yes.

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.030
Let's go, too!

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.050
Okay, Aniki!

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:27.170
That is not necessary.

00:13:28.050 --> 00:13:30.680
This time, Tohma and Gaomon are best for the job.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:32.890
No way!

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:34.680
Yeah! I'll go, too!

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:36.110
That's an order.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:41.120
You should watch how Tohma and Gaomon fight.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:42.640
Yoshino.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:46.440
You and Lalamon will go to support Tohma.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:47.110
Understood!

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:57.530
Gaomon. Five minutes.

00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:58.500
Yes, Master.

00:14:00.660 --> 00:14:02.170
Gaomon, Plan A.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:04.610
Double Backhand!

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:12.610
Plan A-2!

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:17.610
Digisoul Charge!

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.620
Gaomon, evolve!

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:38.290
Gaogamon!

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:41.330
Take them down in one stroke!

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:45.520
Spiral Blow!

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:51.830
Well done!

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:54.010
Perfect teamwork, just like always!

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.980
3 minutes, 47 seconds.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.290
We shortened it by another minute.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.710
Yes, Master.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:04.110
There are two PetitMeramon in Area B-17!

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.210
Gaomon, you're up again.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:08.070
Yes, Master.

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:11.570
It's as if he wasn't even gone for half a year.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.250
That's our Tohma-sama!

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:17.650
His clever, lightning-fast techniques look great!

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.080
Wow...

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:22.420
Understand now?

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:26.250
This is the difference in ability between you and Tohma.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.080
Aniki!

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.490
Aren't you going to stop him?

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:36.390
Leave him alone.

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:41.810
Aniki...

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:43.810
Why are you angry?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:44.910
Shut up!

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:49.530
Damn it...

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:54.150
Well, I think Tohma and Gaomon are nasty guys too, but...

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:56.550
No...

00:15:57.050 --> 00:16:01.240
It's myself that I'm mad at, not them.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.330
Damn it!

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:04.420
What am I doing?

00:16:05.180 --> 00:16:08.370
Really... what the hell am I doing?

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.550
Oh no!

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:22.830
Old man!

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:25.310
What're you doing in a place like this?

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.890
Just what it looks like, making a fire.

00:16:27.890 --> 00:16:29.540
I'm cooking fish.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.340
It's hard lighting up a fire...

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:37.370
The sparks go out easily whenever the wind gets even a little too strong.

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.240
Well, obviously!

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:49.460
But... once I get a larger flame going, it burns stronger no matter how much the wind blows.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:53.090
Fire is an interesting thing, isn't it?

00:16:55.900 --> 00:16:57.370
This is...

00:16:59.100 --> 00:16:59.830
Tohma!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:01.600
Digimon signals in Area B-42!

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:03.470
What?!

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:05.270
Aren't there gas tanks over there?!

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.980
It'll be 10 minutes before we get there!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:10.980
Leave it to me!

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:13.890
What are you saying?

00:17:13.890 --> 00:17:14.910
You can't do it!

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:15.920
Shut up!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.870
I can get there in 3 minutes!

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:20.720
Let's go, Agumon!

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.160
Right, Aniki!

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.700
I won't approve of this!

00:17:29.700 --> 00:17:31.330
Whatever, just watch!

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:33.380
I'll get 'em this time!

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:37.090
This is the worst...

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:40.550
He'll never be able to secure the PetitMeramon.

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.180
Agumon!

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:48.900
Use Baby Burner!

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.570
Is he planning to blow up the gas tanks?!

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:54.570
Don't be a fool!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.530
That's not the only problem. To begin with...

00:17:56.990 --> 00:18:00.520
My attacks don't work on them!

00:18:00.520 --> 00:18:01.800
You heard me, do it!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.400
Okay...

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:05.910
Baby Burner!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:10.720
More!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.160
Baby Burner!

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:15.660
Baby Burner!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.020
Baby Burner!

00:18:22.800 --> 00:18:24.100
Evolve!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.290
Meramon!

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.290
It evolved! What now, Aniki?!

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.170
This is perfect!

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:37.890
Come on.

00:18:37.890 --> 00:18:38.990
Do your worst!

00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:42.890
Aniki...

00:18:43.680 --> 00:18:48.140
Fire sparks easily go out whenever the wind blows on them.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:48.990
But...

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:54.230
Once they burst into flame...!

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:00.590
Aniki!

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:10.730
They won't be extinguished that easily!

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:12.190
Aniki!

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.580
Digisoul Charge!

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:21.480
Agumon, evolve!

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:27.810
<b>mou nani mo nai sekai ja kandou dekinai</b>

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:27.810
<b>A world that's full of nothing can't inspire anyone</b>

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:32.770
<b>sou, kizuita sono hi kara wakaru no sa</b>

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:32.770
<b>You'll understand what I mean after the day you realize that</b>

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.880
<b>furue wo tomete</b>

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.880
<b>Stop your trembling</b>

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.500
<b>hitomi wo hirake</b>

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.500
<b>Open your eyes</b>

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.380
GeoGreymon!

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:43.310
<b>kimi no jikan wo tokihanate!</b>

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:43.310
<b>And liberate your time!</b>

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.990
He got it to evolve on purpose...

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:43.720
by making the fire stronger...

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.270
<b>mirai e Shootin' star!</b>

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.270
<b>Oh shootin' star to the future!</b>

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:50.560
<b>hikari no aachi egake</b>

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:50.560
<b>Draw an arch of light</b>

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:51.100
Go!

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:55.830
<b>todoku no sa shinjitsuzukeru naraba</b>

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:55.830
<b>As long as you keep believing, it'll reach up there</b>

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.200
Mega Burst!

00:19:56.080 --> 00:20:01.630
<b>kimi wo yobu koe ga kokoro de hajiketara</b>

00:19:56.080 --> 00:20:01.630
<b>When the voice that calls you bellows with the heart</b>

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:07.800
<b>subete ga hajimaru Believer!</b>

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:07.800
<b>That's when everything will begin, Believer!</b>

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:05.680
Yeah!

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:09.120
Overpowering Meramon's flames...

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.200
What power...

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.750
All of the Digimon signals are gone!

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:16.920
Not bad!

00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:26.630
How's that?

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:29.310
I was able to take out the PetitMeramon, too!

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:32.510
Don't let this go to your head.

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:34.480
You were just lucky this time.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:37.470
It's just like I told you,

00:20:37.470 --> 00:20:40.490
the ones who don't give up until the end win the fight!

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:43.540
Don't be absurd.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:45.490
You don't even come up with any strategy or tactics.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:48.450
Do you think using force all the time will let you win at everything?

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:52.230
Hah, sounds like a sore loser to me.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.200
What did you say?

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:55.090
Wanna make somethin' of it?

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:59.060
I'll knock you out with one hit to the face this time!

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.630
Don't be stupid. Just because you won with luck once...

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:02.880
CUT IT OUT!

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:08.090
There it is.

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:10.300
I haven't heard that thunderous demon roar of his in a long time...

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.730
Masaru. Tohma.

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:16.100
From now on, you two will be a team.

00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:20.160
You want me... to act alongside him?

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:21.560
You're joking!

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:24.840
I'll never accept him as my partner!

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.280
That is an order.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:32.580
This is the worst...

